posts.body:
I already have enough understanding to make maps, events, control self switches, variables, animations etc but i'm not sure what is possible within the engine. My biggest problem is scripting and terminology tied to javascript and MZ.
I'll try be more specific with the issue.
Using EliMZ_SelfVariables with EliMZ_Book, but they don't appear to be working.
I'm trying to set this up using the lowest # of variables possible.  I want ore nodes to respawn every 20ish minutes or so and not reset when player leaves the map and returns.  I have a common event that ticks up a globalTime variable every 60 frames (1 second).
I'd like to have a way to set a timestamp variable of when the node was harvested without a global variable for each node.
ChatGPT had me set up this on page 1 and 2.  I semi-understand what its trying to do, but not sure if it's possible or remotely correct.
Page 1 before setting self switch on (to make event despawn), +10 seconds for testing:
var index = $gameMap.mapId() * 1000 + this.eventId();
$gameVariables.setValue(index, $gameSystem._globalTime + 10);
page 2 to respawn the event:
var i = $gameMap.mapId() * 1000 + this.eventId();
if ($gameSystem._globalTime >= $gameVariables.value(i)) {  $gameSelfSwitches.setValue([$gameMap.mapId(), this.eventId(), "A"], false);
}
I'm fairly certain that I can accomplish what I'm aiming for if I set up a variable for each node for the time in seconds it was harvested plus 1200 seconds, then respawn....but I was hoping for a more efficient way without blowing up my brain.
